  "measurementLimits": [
    "Each study uses three samples per source or variant, scenario and CPU-throttle rate. Preserve medians with their minimum/maximum ranges; these are not confidence intervals, p95/p99 values or physical-device guarantees.",
    "Compare only the embedded same-host baseline/candidate pair or the same-host in-bounds/OOB pair within its own study. Qualified PERF24 and the later diagnostic use different browser versions/host records; do not compare their absolute timings as a paired experiment.",
    "syncMs measures the synchronous JavaScript event. firstFrameAfterMs and frameGapMs are CPU render-loop completion markers from RelayPerfProbe.framePresented, not GPU-completion fences or display-scanout latency.",
    "Phase components may overlap their parents. Combined static time is computed per record without parent/child double counting; diagnostic attribution scopes are nonadditive. A cheaper read call or static scope does not prove that work disappeared.",
    "The native evidence qualifies the recorded Chromium/ANGLE llvmpipe environments. An in-bounds pixel read is also not a standards-defined whole-canvas GPU fence."
